# TypeScript Type Imports/Exports

When working with TypeScript files in this project, please prefer using type-only imports and exports whenever you are dealing exclusively with types or interfaces.

-   Use `import type { MyType } from './my-module';` instead of `import { MyType } from './my-module';`.
-   Use `export type { MyType } from './my-module';` instead of `export { MyType } from './my-module';` when re-exporting types.
-   Use `export type { MyInterfaceOrType }` instead of `export { MyInterfaceOrType }` when exporting a type or interface definition.

This practice helps maintain clean code and is often necessary when the `isolatedModules` TypeScript compiler option is enabled, which is common in modern projects. Adhering to this helps prevent potential build or runtime issues.
